# Project: notesapp (The Chronicler)

- Purpose: Self-hosted D&D / TTRPG party notes, journal, and knowledge graph app
- Stack: Node/Express + SQLite backend; React (Vite) frontend; Docker
- Location on server: ~/notesapp
- Container name(s): dnd-chronicler (compose service `chronicler`)
- Internal port: 3001 (published on host; Cloudflare Tunnel `notes.ejhomelabs.me` → localhost:3001)
- Health check: http://dnd-chronicler:3001/health (or localhost:3001/health)
- Public route: https://notes.ejhomelabs.me/
- Auth: app JWT (login/register). Remember me → 90d JWT in localStorage; else 12h in sessionStorage. Not behind Cloudflare Access.
- Persistent data: Docker volume `notesapp_chronicler_data` → `/data` (DB + uploads). Backed up with scripts/backup.sh; nightly host job `~/bin/backup-chronicler.sh` also runs.
- Deploy: scripts/deploy.sh (legacy `./deploy.sh` wraps it)
- Env vars: see `.env.example` (`JWT_SECRET`; optional `RECAP_MODEL` / `RECAP_EXTRACT_MODEL` / `RECAP_WRITE_MODEL` / `RECAP_VERIFY_MODEL`, `GLOSSARY_SCAN_MODEL`, `APP_TIMEZONE`, `RECAP_DEBUG`; others auto-generated into `/data` on first boot)
- GitHub repo: EAJ-97/The-Chronicler (private); folder name is `notesapp`

